jobs.description:
Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!

Are you looking for a varied role in the manufacturing industry? Then we’re looking for you to work for a client in Ittervoort. This is a position as an operator on the mixing line, working in a 3-shift rotation. This means you’ll be responsible for assembling orders. You’ll ensure that the logistics process runs smoothly and that everything is put together properly. Your daily responsibilities will include the following:

- You’ll create the correct combinations and place the products together in the packaging;
- You’ll check that the packages are complete and undamaged as they’re loaded onto the pallets;
- Occasionally moving products with a forklift.

This is a three-shift position, Monday through Friday. You will work the following shifts: 5:54 a.m.–2:00 p.m., 1:54 p.m.–10:00 p.m., 9:54 p.m.–6:00 a.m. (7.36 paid hours).

- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You have experience with production work;
- You have experience operating a forklift.
- Would you like to further your career in production? Then we’re looking for you!

Are you welcoming, organised and do you enjoy making sure everything in the office runs smoothly? For our client in Amsterdam, we are looking for an office coordinator who enjoys taking a hands-on approach and combining a variety of responsibilities. As an office coordinator, you and your colleagues ensure a welcoming and well-organised working environment. You combine reception and general office duties with administrative and logistics support. You are the main point of contact at the office and independently make sure everything runs smoothly. Your responsibilities include:  - Welcoming employees, visitors and external partners;
 - Providing reception and front desk support;
 - Carrying out administrative tasks;
 - Coordinating lunch, deliveries and suppliers;
 - Coordinating repair and maintenance requests;
 - Processing orders and preparing shipping documents and labels;
 - Supporting the Office Manager with day-to-day activities.


Wij bieden
  - A gross hourly wage of €17.31;
 - A part-time position for 20-24 hours per week;
 - Flexible working hours and days;
 - A varied position within an international working environment;
 - Plenty of independence and responsibility;
 - An enthusiastic and committed team in Amsterdam.



 - Has an MBO/HBO level of education and thinking;
 - Is welcoming, friendly and service-oriented;
 - Works in an organised and accurate manner;
 - Has a good command of English and preferably communicates well in Dutch;
 - Is available around lunchtime from Monday to Thursday and for the full day on Friday;
 - Is flexible and occasionally available for additional hours during holidays or sick leave.
